  "description": "The 2026 Tennessee gubernatorial election is an open-seat race to succeed term-limited Republican Governor Bill Lee, who cannot seek a third consecutive term. The Republican primary field is led by U.S. Senator Marsha Blackburn, who has strong name recognition and endorsements from President Donald Trump and key conservative groups, facing U.S. Representative John Rose and state Representative Monty Fritts. On the Democratic side, Memphis City Councilwoman Jerri Green is the only candidate who has previously won elected office, running against several other Democratic contenders including former gubernatorial candidate Carnita Atwater, pastor Kevin Lee McCants, and musician Adam \"Ditch\" Kurtz. Tennessee has not elected a Democrat to statewide office since 2006, making the race heavily Republican-favored in the general election. The primary elections are scheduled for August 6, 2026.",
